entries.definition_en:
παλινγενεσία (Rec. παλιγγ-), -ας, ἡ 
 (πάλιν, γενεσις), 
new birth, renewal, restoration, regeneration; 
 __(a) of persons (Plut., Phil., al.), of spiritual regeneration, διὰ λουτροῦ παλινγενεστίας (genitive attr., see Ellic., in l), Tit.3:5; 
 __(b) of the world, as in Stoics, Jewish Apocal., al. (see Dalman, Words, 177 ff.), Mat.19:28.†
 (AS)

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.8; also translated "men"; 
 § Gabbai = "my back"
 the head of an important Benjamite family living in Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah

A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.24; 
 son of: Shashak (H8349); 
 brother of: Ishpan (H3473), Eber (H5677J), Eliel (H0447I), Abdon (H5658I), Zichri (H2147I), Hanan (H2605), Hananiah (H2608O), Elam (H5867), Iphdeiah (H3301) and Penuel (H6439I) 
 § Antothijah = "Jehovah's answer"
 a Benjamite, one of the sons of Jeroham

A man of the tribe of Ephraim living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.25; 
 son of: Beriah (H1283H); 
 brother of: Sheerah (H7609) and Rephah (H7506); 
 father of: Telah (H8520) 
 § Resheph = "flame"
 a son of Ephraim
